#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""console-api — the thin management backend the ttyd rewrite dropped (P1).

Serves the /api the SPA needs to be a real console: live VM state, power
actions, keeper launch/status, and a health view that makes the silent
comms failures visible. Port of the disabled console/server.py ACTIONS —
reuse, don't reinvent (CONSOLE-OVERHAUL.md §3B).

Security model:
  - binds 127.0.0.1 only; nginx fronts it under the authed, LAN-allowed
    console vhost.
  - POSTs require the X-Console header (browsers won't attach custom
    headers cross-origin without CORS, so this kills drive-by CSRF).
  - VM names validated against a strict regex AND the live `lxc list`.
  - PROTECTED VMs (same set as keeper-broker) refuse stop/restart; start
    is always allowed — powering ON is additive.
  - every action appends to the shared control-audit.jsonl.

Stdlib only (http.server + subprocess) — no venv to rot.
"""
